// Title: Assembly Loading Via CL_LoadAssembly.ps1
// Sigma ID: c57872c7-614f-4d7f-a40d-b78c8df2d30d
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-05-21 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1216
// Description: Detects calls to "LoadAssemblyFromPath" or "LoadAssemblyFromNS" that are part of the
//   "CL_LoadAssembly.ps1" script. This can be abused to load different assemblies and bypass App
//   locker controls.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://bohops.com/2018/01/07/executing-commands-and-bypassing-applocker-with-powershell-diagnostic-scripts/
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Scripts/CL_LoadAssembly/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_powershell_cl_loadassembly.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "LoadAssemblyFromPath " or ProcessCommandLine contains "LoadAssemblyFromNS "
